        "id": 241484,
        "name": "KateWalker",
        "username": "TakeWalker",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/{size}/5677_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-11-30T17:07:24.227Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Christopher’s not eating the world before I do. I’m taking this as a personal challenge. &gt;:B</p>\n<p>The tense change they are looking for is “smote”, which I think is a hilarious word myself.</p>\n<p>Ooh, two issues in one here!</p>\n<p>Hey! I’ve made that “Adam and Christopher Readingletterstoyou” joke before! &gt;:V</p>\n<p>Oh man, I really want a multi-religious Fanatic story now. “A bad issue/arc” is something I’ve wanted for a Writer’s Room for a long time, and either that story or the Tokenized Adepts are the best candidates so far.</p>\n<p>Well’p, so much for getting that Anheuser-Busch sponsorship!</p>\n<p>“You made your bed, now burn in it” is one of the most badass lines I have ever heard, I hope that gets used somewhere.</p>\n<p>Ooh, Vince Snyder stuff on the horizon. I’ll always take a tease when an answer isn’t right. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=10\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\"></p>\n<p>So if we filled the sandwich bag with Diet Coke, would the jelly dissolve in it? V:</p>\n<p>I am not sure if I want to know why Adam had a raccoon in his freezer. c.c For all that “Did you ever eat that raccoon?” is a hell of a way to begin a conversation.</p>\n<p>I want this recipe for candied cranberries. c.c I adore cranberry sauce in all its forms, and this sounds amazing.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-11-30T17:07:24.227Z",
