        "raw": "Christopher's not eating the world before I do. I'm taking this as a personal challenge. >:B\n\nThe tense change they are looking for is \"smote\", which I think is a hilarious word myself.\n\nOoh, two issues in one here!\n\nHey! I've made that \"Adam and Christopher Readingletterstoyou\" joke before! >:V\n\nOh man, I really want a multi-religious Fanatic story now. \"A bad issue/arc\" is something I've wanted for a Writer's Room for a long time, and either that story or the Tokenized Adepts are the best candidates so far.\n\nWell'p, so much for getting that Anheuser-Busch sponsorship!\n\n\"You made your bed, now burn in it\" is one of the most badass lines I have ever heard, I hope that gets used somewhere.\n\nOoh, Vince Snyder stuff on the horizon. I'll always take a tease when an answer isn't right. :D\n\nSo if we filled the sandwich bag with Diet Coke, would the jelly dissolve in it? V:\n\nI am not sure if I want to know why Adam had a raccoon in his freezer. c.c For all that \"Did you ever eat that raccoon?\" is a hell of a way to begin a conversation.\n\nI want this recipe for candied cranberries. c.c I adore cranberry sauce in all its forms, and this sounds amazing.",
