        "id": 241495,
        "name": "",
        "username": "The_Justifier",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_justifier/{size}/4954_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-12-01T18:09:22.689Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So the story was neat, but the intentional decision to avoid resolving it bums me out.  It’s certainly realistic as a comics industry practice, but if this comic actually existed, the incredibly badass cover would sucker me into buying it, and then I’d feel cheated when it turned out to be the middle of a story with no beginning or end.  This is certainly an experience which meta-metaverse comics have inflicted on me, but I do tend to prefer when C&amp;A go for “let’s do it our way which is better” instead of\"let’s do it the way it actually would have happened in the Eighties\".</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
